    "parameter_convention": "The fixed sufficient constant is 1/1000 for both ratios. The natural floor of a supplies the actual integer joining-degree bound. The ratio theorem assumes h>0; undivided variants cover h=0."
  },
  "scope": "Full Lemma 4.15 for finite loopless multigraphs, hence also simple graphs. All inputs refer to the original graph: h-regularity, no h-overfull set, four odd label fibers, actual joining degree at most real a, a prescribed perfect matching or three-edge star with at least r0 actual copies on every prescribed pair, and the manuscript forest-cut supply. The explicit sufficient conditions are a/h <= 1/1000 and (h-r0)/h <= 1/1000 for h>0. The output is an exact partition of the actual joining-copy subtype into actual matchings, exactly h with injective perfect-matching/star projection; every surplus projection is a two-edge circuit. The stronger undivided variants need only individual pair supplies and cover h=0. All quotient cuts/parities, finite selections and matching constructions are derived. This is a direct alternative proof; the general compatible-circuit theorem and terminal factorization are not claimed.",
